  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the negligible difference in outcomes and the comparison of probabilities of achieving a favorable (i.e., non-zero) outcome — aligns with what the individual considered. The individual acknowledges the small outcome difference and treats it as unimportant, matching the reason’s premise. They also focus on the risk of getting nothing, effectively comparing the likelihood of a favorable (non-zero) outcome, and favor the option with certainty (Lottery B). Their justification mirrors the rule of the decision reason: when outcomes are similar, prefer the one with higher probability of a favorable result. Despite a slip in naming the lotteries at the end, the reasoning structure is consistent with the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
